                "text": "The rule: keep the most frequent color, everything else gray (5).\n\nLet me create demonstration pairs. The example given: 8 appears 4 times, 7 appears 5 times, so 7 is most frequent. Output keeps 7, others become 5.\n\nNote tie-breaking: argmax picks max by size. If tie... max returns first encountered in iteration order of frozenset, which is unpredictable. Better to avoid ties.\n\nLet me produce several varied pairs without ties.\n\nPair 1: 3x3 grid with color counts distinct.\n\nLet me design:\n- [[1,1,1],[1,2,2],[3,3,3]] : count 1:4, 2:2, 3:3 \u2192 most 1 (4). Output: 1 kept, others 5.\n\nActually let's make varied sizes and colors.\n\nPair A (2x2): [[0,4],[4,4]] \u2192 4 count 3, 0 count 1. Most 4. Output [[5,4],[4,4]].\n\nPair B (4x3): colors 2 (count 6), 6 (count 3), 9 (count 3)? tie between 6 and 9 \u2014 avoid. Let's do 6 count 4, 9 count 2.\n\nLet me just do a set of clear ones.\n\nPair 1: [[1,1,1],[1,2,2],[3,3,3]] \u2014 counts: 1\u21924, 2\u21922, 3\u21923. Winner 1.\n\nPair 2: [[0,4],[4,4]] \u2014 winner 4.\n\nPair 3: 4x4 grid: color 3 in a big region, others small.\n\nLet me build: \nrow0: 3 3 3 3\nrow1: 3 7 7 3\nrow2: 3 7 7 3\nrow3: 3 3 3 3\ncounts: 3\u219212, 7\u21924. Winner 3.\n\nPair 4: [[5,5],[8,5],[8,8],[8,5]] 4 rows 2 cols. counts: 5\u21925, 8\u21923. Winner 5.\n\nHmm vary colors beyond. Let me include color 5 itself? If most common color is 5, nothing changes except others become 5... fine but confusing maybe. Skip.\n\nPair 5: single row: [[9,9,9,1,1]] \u2192 9\u21923, 1\u21922. Winner 9. Output [[9,9,9,5,5]].\n\nAlso maybe a grid where three colors. Fine.\n\nLet me submit about 5-6 pairs.\n\nI'll call show_transformed_input for each. These are independent, can batch.\n\nLet me double check the argmax tie behavior\u2014avoid ties as noted.\n\nLet me finalize inputs:\n\n1. [[1,1,1],[1,2,2],[3,3,3]]\n2. [[0,4],[4,4]]\n3. [[3,3,3,3],[3,7,7,3],[3,7,7,3],[3,3,3,3]]\n4. [[5,5],[8,5],[8,8],[8,5]]\n5. [[9,9,9,1,1]]\n6. [[2,6,6,6],[2,2,6,6],[2,2,2,6]] counts 2:6? row0: 2,6,6,6 \u2192 2:1,6:3; row1: 2,2,6,6 \u21922:2,6:2; row2: 2,2,2,6 \u21922:3,6:1. Total 2:6, 6:6. Tie! Bad. Change row2 to 2,2,2,2: total 2:7, 6:5. Input [[2,6,6,6],[2,2,6,6],[2,2,2,2]] counts 2:7, 6:5. Winner 2.\n\nGood, 6 pairs. Let's submit.",
